  "details": "FYI: sry I threw both requests into the same post, will clean that up/seperate them after catching some sleep!\n\n.\n\nGot 2 (imo) sm0l but QOL-effective CAM-features in the back of my mind since forever - maybe now, as devs are working on the cam-code bc animoji anyways - might be an opportunity to consider implementing these? TIA <3\n\n1 - burst shot-mode: have the 5s timer \"stick\" so the CAM basically takes image-series. every x seconds a new shot (1-5s would be great time intervals imo) so you actually have your hands free\n\n2 - stream-cam: add the option to NOT show the ingame camera seek-UI (toggle to hide/unhide it after you set your cams-pov), as it is quite resource-heavy when being rendered onscreen.\n\nand - when dancing/twirling around (see vid) I cannot find a place to park the cam-UI so it does NOT a) annoy me when in my POV and b) DOES safe a few fps - which could make the difference between fluid 60fps recording or dropping below & lag\n\nthx @artemus for getting me to describe in detail ;)\n\nthoughts?\n\n.\n\nTLDRs\n\nBurstShot: Automatically trigger a photo every 'user-selectable timeframe (~3-5 predefined values)' until manual stopping (or the storage-device is full [*bursts*])\n\nStreamCAM: there IS a way to get 5-10% additional frametime \"reserve/headroom\" out of our current rigs - for FREE - (not) rendering the streamcams UI could be exactly that reserve for full-load situations \n\n.\n\n.\n\ndiscord threads: https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/449386885299830794/1228904329361100921\n\nhttps://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/337673877553545229/1228910949927354420",
